&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;
mso-bidi-font-weight:bold&quot;&gt;Condition: Unless discharged under planning permission&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Arial, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 13.3333px;&quot;&gt;23/P2064&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;, prior&amp;nbsp;
to the commencement of development, a detailed scheme for the provision
of surface and foul water drainage shall be submitted to and approved in
writing by the local planning authority for the development. The drainage
scheme will dispose of surface water by means of a sustainable drainage system
(SuDS) and to include a green roof at the agreed runoff rate (no more than 1
l/s), in accordance with drainage hierarchy contained within the London Plan Policy
(SI 13 and SPG) and the advice contained within the National SuDS Standards.
The drainage design and plans shall include pipe sizes and direction of flow
and positively pumped devices and non-return valves to prevent back up of flow.
The scheme shall include SuDS measures, such as raingardens, permeable paving
and geo-cellular storage or agreed suitable SuDS alternatives. Where such details have been discharged under planning permission&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Arial, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 13.3333px;&quot;&gt;23/P2064, they shall be complied with in full in respect of this permission.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;
